# CI runner logs, timings, and the leak record (scripts/run_suites.py).
.ci-logs/

# A local copy of a retired mockup, dropped in the repo root to view a page
# beside it. `the-living-garden.html` was DELETED on purpose in #56 — it had
# shipped, never deployed, and its retirement is what caught the guard that
# exempted garden.html from the index rule. It came back in #58 because a
# reference copy was sitting untracked in the working tree when a `git add -A`
# ran, which is the whole reason this line exists: the file is a reference to
# look at, never a file this repo carries.
#
# Mockups live in `mockups/` now, which is what keeps them off the served
# site: the deploy is `cp ./*.html _site/`, so a page is published by being at
# the ROOT. This one is ignored as well as unserved, because it is a local
# copy of a retired file rather than one the repo keeps.
mockups/the-living-garden.html

# Scratch working documents from the superpowers skill set (brainstorms,
# plans, specs produced while shaping a build before it has one). Not this
# repo's documentation — that lives directly under docs/ (annotation-scope.md,
# error-messages.md) and a handful of docs/superpowers/ files already tracked
# from past builds, which this does not untrack. This only keeps FUTURE
# scratch drops out of `git status`.
docs/superpowers/
